From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Windows: CromIKO settings and weekly shield report

"CromIKO" at the top of Settings on the desktop, with the mascot, like the
CromIKO settings of the Android app (CromIKO-Settings.patch): Settings open
on it, and it is the first item of the menu.

- A card with the mascot at the top, then the CromIKO features in groups,
  each with its icon from the logo (the star in the accent color):
  - Protection: CromIKO DNS (with its status), the pop-up guard, ad
    blocking (Adblock Plus) and the weekly shield report (with the count
    of the week).
  - Privacy: the Fire button, with a button that burns the tabs and data
    right away (after its dialog).
  - Look and feel: the accent colors and the new tab page, which open
    Customize CromIKO.
  - Downloads: the CromIKO download manager.
- The settings stay where Chromium has them too: the rows open them.

The weekly shield report is a page of the section (chrome://settings/
cromiko/report), like on Android (CromIKO-Shield-Report.patch), from the
same counts (cromiko_shield_stats.cc):

- The ads and trackers blocked this week, compared with the same days of
  last week (Monday to yesterday), and last week's total.
- A bar for each day from Monday to Sunday, with its count, today in the
  accent color.
- The 5 sites where CromIKO blocked the most, with their favicons, and the
  5 trackers and ad servers it blocked the most, each with a bar of its
  part; early in the week, last week's lists.
- The ad blocker settings, and where the report is kept.

The shield card of the new tab page now opens the report.

